Z||000003||Cooter||07-20-99||08:09 PM||||My v6 parts car has got a low mileage motor- less than 40,000 and you can get the whole car plus another complete 85 coupe for $800.
Z||000004||batboy||07-20-99||08:52 PM||||You could always get a remanufactured long block 2.8 or a short block 3.1 and have your old heads rebuilt at a machine shop, then use all the external stuff off your old engine.<p>Having a smaller shop do the work if you can't or don't want to change engines, rather than the dealership would save you mega bucks. I bet you could be driving your Fiero again for at least 1/2 the price of that $3000 (choke) quote from Pontiac. Heck, for that price, you could buy another nice Fiero. That's why I avoid the dealerships like the plague.<p>For $3000 you could buy a high performance 3.4 crate motor, have Ed Parks swap it in for you and still have plenty of change left over. Around here you can buy a good used engine and get it installed for about $1000. Don't give up hope, explore all your options.<p>That offer of Cooter's sounds like a bargain. If he didn't live so far away, I'd hook up my flatbed trailer and go pick it up myself. I recently found an 85 Fiero in good shape and the engine ran good, but the clutch was out of it. He wanted $500 for it, I offered $400 for it but another guy ended up buying it for his asking price.<p>Look around, ask around, the deals are out there, you just have to believe. Oh no, I'm being to sound like the X-Files!<p>Check out this URL. This is not an endorsement, I've never actually done business with this company, it's just an example of remanufactured engines and prices.<p>http://www.bluechipmotor.com/<p>
Z||000005||lowCG||07-20-99||11:23 PM||||Yeah,these guys speak the truth,after this many years of being out of production,the dealer isn't going to provide any better service than a decent shop,just the prices from when it was a new car.Dealers use aftermarket parts just like the other shops for something that old.<br>Low mile,guaranteed junkyard motors are even getting harder to find,still out there though.
Z||000006||JetroGT||07-21-99||12:14 AM||||RS motorsports out of Canada sells remanufactured long blocks for the Fiero in 2.8 and 3.3 L versions. They want $1450 Canaidan for the 2.8 and $1535 for the 3.3L<br>http://webhome.idirect.com/~rsm1/<br>I've got two extra 2.8's, one that I am rebuilding to replace my high miles 2.8. The other is in a burnt out 86 GT that I bought as a parts car. <br>
Z||000007||Racer 1||07-21-99||01:18 AM||||Gokart I feel ya pain.I was sitting back here and thinking how you could still drive you fiero without a running engine till you buy a new engine... 1. Once a month call a towing place to tow your car with you in it around town.  2.Have your friends push you around the street and act like your going fast in the car. 3. Get some geto dogs to pull your car 4 free like a snow sled. 4.Take pictures of your inside interior and then get them blown up and put them in your room on the walls. Dang you must be depressed right now. GOOD LUCK  P.S. My fiero is running fine.im having fun driving around getting the ladies to turn there heads and look at my hot car.Ill post when it breaks down!
Z||000008||ChadMan||07-21-99||07:45 AM||||Batboy's right - I'd call Ed Parks.  He really knows Fieros, he's got a lot of good engines lying around, and he won't try to rob you blind.  Who knows, maybe you'd get lucky and get away with new heads on your old block.  Depending on where you are, he might even be willing to come get your car with a flatbed.<p>You've got to do something, GoKart.  The thought of a fellow Fiero nut having to ride around with his girlfriend/wife, or take the bus, well...it kinda makes me want to cry.
Z||000009||Gokart||07-21-99||07:15 PM||||Thanks for all your condolences guys! If it's ok with you I might wanna hang out here still even though I'm sure to have an undrivable Fiero soon! I will weigh out my options and figure out what to do. I will try Ed Parks, I'm figuring it may be better to save some cash and put a low miles engine in it instead of possibly wasting any more with this one.
